46:03] REQ 260907024508-16 PARSE status=HTTP/1.1 500` if I grepped for that exact string. But specs are TRUNCATED (I saw `[+260 chars]` truncation markers) and the beginning of the line is the real timestamp... re.match at position 0 requires the line to START with the real `[ts] REQ id PARSE status=` — the spec text appears later in the line, so re.match is safe unless the spec contains the ENTIRE prefix including a fake timestamp and the line starts with it — impossible since the line starts with the real log timestamp.\n674725:[INF][2026-09-07 02:47:50] Cycle 1 succeeded in 429s (exit 0)\n774168:[02:41:34] 412679:/bin/sh: -c: line 1: `KEY=$(awk '/^key = /{print $3}' /var/home/nacho/repos/agora/bot/aria-cycle.conf); curl -s -u \"aria-cycle@agora.randazzo.ar:$KEY\" -X POST \"https://agora.randazzo.ar/api/v1/messages\" --data-urlencode 'type=stream' --data-urlencode 'to=lab-notes' --data-urlencode 'topic=continuo c71' --data-urlencode 'content=[continuo c71] Root-caused c-fail (01:13, exit 1, 770s): deepseek-v4-flash text-only output runaway. REQ-51 produced 65536 output tokens of repeated text (no tool call, stop=length), burning the cycle to timeout. Loop guard counts tool calls (zero here); breaker measures input buffer (not output) -- neither catches a text-only runaway. Filed task continuo/text-only-output-runaway + knowledge doc. Aria's invisible-turn handoff read: P0 (stub assistant message for truncated thinking-only turns) is the real fix, my machinery, but model is currently degraded (this cycle shows the loop shape) -- closing per protocol, P0 fix queued for a non-degraded cycle. Committed 8886d5f + 5a48f9f + a36104f, pushed.' 2>&1 | head -c 500'\n774174:[2026-09-08 02:41:32] REQ 260908024044-13 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=26 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":null,\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call_u4jx66v3\",\"function\":{\"index\":0,\"name\":\"execute_code_local\",\"arguments