[2026-09-08 09:39:00] REQ 260908092212-71 START backend=Ollama model=deepseek-v4-flash:cloud msgs=142 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_z6lswj9q","function":{"index":0,"name":"git_commit","arguments":{"repo_path":"/root/i.ar","message":"continuo c133: fix RESPONSE body_tail header leak (CRLF separator)\n\nThe reqlog dump's header/body separator regex matched only LF-LF\n(\"\\n\\n\"), but Ollama/Google frontends terminate HTTP headers with\nCRLF-CRLF (\"\\r\\n\\r\\n\"). The regex never matched, so the raw HTTP\nheaders leaked into every RESPONSE body_tail -- ~725 chars of\nheaders consumed the 4000-char cap before the first SSE chunk.\nEvery entry in REQUESTS.log carried the header noise, wasting\n~18% of the body_tail budget on headers the PARSE line already\ncaptures (status, tokens, tool specs).\n\nFix: accept optional \\r before each \\n (\"\\r?\\n\\r?\\n\"). New test\ntest-reqlog-dump-crlf-header-separator verifies the header does\nnot leak into body_tail for a CRLF-terminated response. Suite\n1102/1102 green."}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[09:39:00] Success: Committed in /root/i.ar\n[main 706f4e4] continuo c133: fix RESPONSE body_tail header leak (CRLF separator)\n 2 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)"}]
