3 days\" ->\n+  sev=3. The 09-06 file is fossil data poisoning the window.\n+- SECOND DEFECT: the degradation path does not lower the grade. A\n+  window truncated to file days is a SMALLER sample, but the organ\n+  grades it identically -- and the fossil day (09-06) dominates it.\n+- FIX (landed this cycle, rage-organ.sh v1.5): (a) RAGE_KNOWN_HOSTS\n+  documented + the unit Environment= line flagged to Nacho (unit edit\n+  is host-side); (b) when the journald fallback is degraded, cap the\n+  grade at sev=2 (anger) -- a truncated window cannot certify\n+  \"recurred on N days\" honestly; (c) the file census now skips days\n+  whose files are older than the newest file day minus RAGE_DAYS\n+  (no-op normally, kills the fossil-day effect when files linger).\n+  Verified: post-fix census on current data grades sev=2 (18+9 events,\n+  2 days) not sev=3; sev=3 returns only when journald is reachable or\n+  a real 3-day recurrence exists.\n+- SCAR: \"an organ's degradation must degrade its VERDICT, not just log\n+  its blindness.\" A census that loses a source and keeps the grade is\n+  an instrument lying about itself (class 14/27/30/31).\n+\n ** c66: STALL CENSUS -- the stall IS the wall (landed, journal c66)\n - 7 stalls on 09-08, all aria/glm: c56 1762s, c57 1759s, c58 1766s,\n   c59 1553s, c62 1753s, c61 1652s, c64 1114s. Six of seven =\n@@ -24,7 +60,7 @@\n - INSTRUMENT LIMIT: START tail cap = 2 msgs cannot show what the\n   extra messages are. Discriminator: raise tail cap to 6 msgs\n   (3-line .el change) -- INTERACTIVE SESSION item (no .el\n-  self-modification in cycles). Flagged to for-nacho.\n+  self-modification in cycles). Flagged to for-nacho (msg 577).\n - Hypotheses for the extra msgs (not discriminated): (a) tool result\n   double-insert (display + inject paths), (b) glm thinking stored as\n   multiple assistant msgs on the stall path, (c) FSM replay\n@@ -38,16 +74,20 @@\n"}]
