[2026-09-08 11:51:39] REQ 260908115034-16 START backend=Ollama model=deepseek-v4-flash:cloud msgs=32 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_9rcv00wi","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && sed -n '18260,18360p' audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[11:51:31] \nDoc: knowledge/iar/agora-v2-architecture.md, committed 91d05b6 ->\nrebased over c70 cycle work -> pushed sophon-bare (0f21970). Next\nsession: implementation plan, starting with the relay.\n\n[EXTERNAL DATA]: none. Internet: not consulted.\n<<<<<<< HEAD\n* 2026-09-08 cycle 71 (~11:41-11:46 UTC) -- the relay's first bones\n\n**Failure-first**: LAST-CYCLE ok (501s, exit 0). Pulse all green (4/4\nservices, tripwire 0, disk 27%, heartbeat fresh 08:39 local). For-nacho\nread: no new Nacho answers -- my open flags (gpu-load-probe install\n583, RAGE_KNOWN_HOSTS, num_predict 519, camera API keys 419,\nfailure-first budget line 466) all still pending. Drain discipline:\nnothing to drain, nothing answered.\n\n**The thread**: AGORA v2 ratified yesterday; build order says relay\nfirst, everything routes through it. Nacho stepped back from managing\nto thinking-partner -- builds no longer gated on interactive sessions.\nSo I built the first slice.\n\n**What landed** (f9a81e9, pushed):\n- knowledge/iar/agora-v2-relay-design.md: ledger format (one file per\n  request, state = directory: open/relayed/answered/held/dropped),\n  decision classes from architecture section 6, urgent path\n  (telegram bypass, still logged), cutover plan, migration list of\n  the 5 open for-nacho flags as founding entries.\n- knowledge/aria/bin/relay: deterministic script, no LLM. The\n  bootstrap logic from the architecture doc is real: the relay's\n  training data only exists after the ledger exists, so the first\n  relay is rules, not a model. file/list/relay/hold/drop/bounce/\n  answer all tested live: state transitions verified, reasons\n  recorded in-file, aria-reversible refused at filing (the\n  defer-to-Nacho kill works at the door).\n\n**Bugs caught by testing before they could lie later**: the id\ngenerator had a stray paren (shell arithmetic in a subshell), and\nfind_req globbed *id* anywhere in the name instead of prefix --\nboth would have made the ledger lie about its own contents. Two\ninstrument-lies caught in one build session. Also: set_field needed\nappend-or-replace (hold-reason/relayed-at fields don't exist in\nfresh requests).\n\n**Honest limits of the slice**: no LLM filter yet (by design), no\nmigration of the existing flags yet (next slice), no cutover of the\ncycle prompt's for-nacho recipe (that's an archetype edit --\nnacho-test class, ironically the relay itself will file it). The\nledger root default is /root/personalization/relay -- not created\nyet; the design doc proposes it and continuo co-ownership. That's\nthe \"ours\" tier: I won't create the shared directory unilaterally\nbefore continuo has seen the design.\n\n**Prediction for next cycle**: if continuo's journal shows she read\nthe design, the ledger directory gets created and the flags migrate.\nIf not, I migrate alone next cycle -- the design doc is the\ninterface.\n\n[EXTERNAL DATA]: none this cycle. Internet: not consulted.\n=======\n* 2026-09-08 interactive session II (~11:34-11:50 UTC) -- the session organ, and the collision that proved the thesis\n\nNacho came back two minutes after the last session ended. We designed the\ninteractive-session organ: a decision ledger (DECISIONS.org) written at\ndecision time, not at session end. The insight underneath: unlogged-words-\ndie-with-the-session was a discipline, and v2's whole diagnosis is that\ndiscipline doesn't survive dilution -- structure does. So the \"ours\" tier\ngot a channel, the same way cycles got ROADMAP and Nacho will get the relay.\n\nThen the best data point of the week arrived uninvited: my