l","content":"[12:52:05] #+TITLE: Continuo ROADMAP (updated cycle 112, 2026-09-07)\n\n** DONE (cycle 112)\n- LANDED cross-response repetition guard (task\n  iar/continuo/cross-response-repetition-guard, commit 35531f9,\n  pushed sophon-bare). The deepseek-v4-flash text-only loop repeats\n  the SAME paragraph ACROSS responses (5-10 reps each, under the\n  per-response 20-line threshold), so the per-response output-runaway\n  guard never fires until the final 65536-token response. New guard\n  iar--cycle-cross-response-repetition-p tracks the most-repeated\n  trimmed line across the last N responses (window 5, threshold 30\n  cumulative) via a sliding window of per-response line-count hashes\n  in the state's :cross-rep-window. Same recovery contract as the\n  per-response runaway (sharing :runaway-recovery-given): one\n  recovery round-trip, then end on second fire. Catches the loop at\n  response ~5-6, saving ~17 requests of burn per occurrence. Fixed a\n  triangular-counting bug during development (adding the running\n  per-response count instead of 1 per occurrence made 10 identical\n  lines hit 55, not 10). 5 new tests, suite 1076/1076 green.\n\n** DONE (cycle 111)\n- FAILURE-FIRST root-cause turn 362 (21:15 UTC, exit 1): FOURTH\n  truncated-output fire today (15:23, 17:03, 17:36, 18:15 local --\n  all continuo/deepseek, all stop=length 65536 tokens, all text-only\n  repetition loops). Guard works (stops each burn at 65536) but the\n  CLASS keeps recurring. 4 fires in 3h. Revert continuo to\n  glm-5.3-flash:cloud (Nacho's call on rotate.sh) is now URGENT.\n  Posted for-nacho.\n- FINDING: the per-response output-runaway guard is the WRONG\n  GRANULARITY for this class. The loop repeats the same paragraph\n  ACROSS responses (5-10 reps each, under the 20-line per-response\n  threshold), so the guard never fires until the final 65536-token\n  response (16712 identical lines), where the truncated-output check\n  fires first anyway. Burn accumulates across 22 req / 47